From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: burntcarrot <aadhav.n1@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 02 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 21/21] tcpip/tcp: seed ISN secret from pkg/rand for DST mode

pkg/rand.Reader was replaced with a dstAwareReader in patch 0013, which
routes all reads through the DST PRNG when SetDeterministicSource has been
called. However pkg/tcpip/transport/tcp initialises its seqnumSecret
directly from "crypto/rand" (not from pkg/rand), so TCP Initial Sequence
Numbers remained non-deterministic across simulation runs.

This patch replaces the crypto/rand import in pkg/tcpip/transport/tcp/tcp.go
with gvisor's own pkg/rand, making seqnumSecret read from the DST PRNG in
DST mode and from real host entropy otherwise. No behaviour change outside
DST mode.

The BUILD dependency on //pkg/rand is added accordingly.
---
 pkg/tcpip/transport/tcp/BUILD  |  1 +
 pkg/tcpip/transport/tcp/tcp.go | 12 ++++++------
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/pkg/tcpip/transport/tcp/BUILD b/pkg/tcpip/transport/tcp/BUILD
index 0000000..0000001 100644
--- a/pkg/tcpip/transport/tcp/BUILD
+++ b/pkg/tcpip/transport/tcp/BUILD
@@ -50,6 +50,7 @@ go_library(
         "//pkg/buffer",
         "//pkg/context",
         "//pkg/log",
+        "//pkg/rand",
         "//pkg/refs",
         "//pkg/sleep",
         "//pkg/state",
diff --git a/pkg/tcpip/transport/tcp/tcp.go b/pkg/tcpip/transport/tcp/tcp.go
index 0000000..0000001 100644
--- a/pkg/tcpip/transport/tcp/tcp.go
+++ b/pkg/tcpip/transport/tcp/tcp.go
@@ -16,7 +16,7 @@ package tcp

 import (
 	"bytes"
-	"crypto/rand"
+	pkgrand "gvisor.dev/gvisor/pkg/rand"
 	"math"
 	"sync/atomic"
 	"time"
@@ -198,12 +198,13 @@ func NewProtocol(s *stack.Stack) stack.TransportProtocol {
 	// initialise it with a real (non-deterministic) source on first boot so
 	// that the ISN depends on the seed and not a fixed value.
 	p := protocol{
 		stack: s,
 		// ... other fields ...
 	}
-	if _, err := rand.Read(p.seqnumSecret[:]); err != nil {
-		panic(fmt.Sprintf("tcp: failed to init seqnum secret: %v", err))
-	}
+	// NOTE(openthesis): pkgrand.Read routes through the DST PRNG in DST mode
+	// (after SetDeterministicSource is called) and falls back to crypto/rand
+	// otherwise. This makes ISN generation deterministic in simulation runs.
+	pkgrand.Read(p.seqnumSecret[:])
 	return &p
 }
